#
# jack.abi — the thread role of a JACK client, declared once (omx-rt-gate(1)). JACK takes its process callback by a
# call (jack_set_process_callback), not by a table, so a client stores the callback in the `process` field of an
# `omx_jack_process` and registers it from that field: the function stored there is the root, judged as audio. The
# one JACK call a process callback may make is jack_port_get_buffer, class host-buffer (classes.tbl, ruled
# 2026-11-15); any other JACK call it reaches is red until a ruling classifies it.
plugin omx_jack_process process audio
